notes.text:
One ending per person is familiar (mangio, mangi, mangia …), but:
- German needs the pronoun (ich esse, not *esse);
- the verb must be second: Vielleicht trinke ich Tee;
- there is no progressive like sto mangiando: Ich esse covers both.

One ending per person is familiar (punoj, punon, punon, punojmë, punoni, punojnë), but:
- German needs the pronoun (ich arbeite, not *arbeite);
- po + verb (po ha) has no German counterpart: Er isst is both “eats” and “is eating”.

Person endings are familiar; new are:
- the obligatory pronoun (ich koche, du kochst);
- the verb in second place whatever comes first (Heute koche ich);
- one present for “I eat” and “I am eating”.
